			"widgets_values":[
				"How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 5.00-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n[Shot 1] Dark fantasy cinematic martial-arts animation with painterly detail and dramatic moonlit blue lighting. Begin exactly from <Picture 1>. Preserve the same adult female swordswoman, facial identity, black hair, dark layered martial-arts costume, flowing red-orange fabric, sword, body proportions, and the same gigantic horned shadow creature. Preserve the moonlit ruined environment, cold blue palette, wet reflective ground, distant traditional architecture, drifting mist, and the established spatial relationship: the swordswoman remains in the foreground-left facing the enormous creature occupying the right side of the frame.\n\nThe swordswoman holds her low combat stance for only a brief instant as her clothing and loose fabric react naturally to the wind. She then drives forcefully forward toward the creature with a fast, grounded martial-arts step, keeping her center of gravity low and her sword under firm control. Her leading foot pushes through the wet ground, producing a small burst of water and debris while her trailing fabric stretches backward from the sudden acceleration.\n\nWithout stopping or changing direction, she converts the forward momentum into one continuous sword attack. Her torso rotates, shoulders and hips turn together, and both arms guide the sword through a broad, powerful sweeping slash. The motion must remain physically connected: forward step → body rotation → sword acceleration → full sweeping strike. Do not introduce additional spins, flips, jumps, unrelated attacks, or extra weapons.\n\nAs the sword reaches maximum speed, a concentrated blue-white energy trail forms directly along the blade path. The energy begins as a narrow luminous streak close to the sword rather than appearing independently. It rapidly expands outward as the slash continues, tracing one large curved crescent through the air. The glowing sword arc sweeps from the swordswoman across the center of the frame toward the gigantic creature, pushing mist, loose particles and surface spray outward along its path.\n\nThe creature remains visually consistent with <Picture 1>: enormous black-blue body, branching horn-like structures, rough spectral texture and glowing red facial markings. It reacts to the incoming strike by leaning and recoiling slightly backward while its upper body and surrounding dark vapor are displaced by the force of the energy wave. Do not transform the creature, change its anatomy, create additional monsters, or make it disappear.\n\nDuring the final phase of the shot, progressively converge toward <Picture 2>. The swordswoman advances from the lower-left foreground into the more central-left position seen in <Picture 2>. Her torso extends into the attack, her sword reaches the exact sweeping orientation of the final frame, and her red-orange trailing fabric stretches backward with the motion. The blue-white sword energy grows into the same dominant luminous crescent shape visible in <Picture 2>, curving around the swordswoman and across the frame toward the creature. The creature, moon, architecture, ground plane and overall framing progressively match the final composition.\n\nAt the 5.00-second mark, land precisely on <Picture 2>: the swordswoman is captured at the peak of the decisive sweeping slash, positioned and oriented exactly as shown in the reference; the enormous blue-white crescent sword wave dominates the middle of the frame; the gigantic horned creature recoils behind it on the upper-right; the full moon remains visible in the upper-left background; and the dark blue ruined environment, water spray, mist, debris, lighting and composition match <Picture 2> as closely as possible.\n\nUse one continuous shot with no cuts. The camera performs a restrained lateral tracking movement following the swordswoman from left toward center while maintaining the creature's massive scale in the background. The camera must not orbit around the characters, perform a dramatic zoom, suddenly change height, or reverse direction. Keep the movement smooth and cinematic so that the transformation from <Picture 1> to <Picture 2> is driven primarily by the swordswoman's attack rather than by camera motion.\n\nMaintain stable character identity, stable facial structure, realistic and coherent limb anatomy, correct hand-to-sword contact, a rigid and clearly defined sword, consistent costume geometry, physically plausible foot placement, coherent body rotation, stable creature anatomy, and consistent environment geometry throughout the entire shot. Preserve the painterly dark-fantasy visual style of both reference images. Use natural directional motion blur only during the fastest sword movement and energy sweep while keeping the swordswoman's face, body silhouette, sword and creature clearly readable.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA cold nighttime wind moves continuously through the ruined environment with faint low-frequency ambience from the gigantic creature. The swordswoman's rapid footwork produces sharp wet impacts and small water splashes, accompanied by fast cloth movement. Her sword produces a clean accelerating metallic whoosh that grows into a powerful sweeping air-cut sound as the blue-white energy arc expands, followed by one deep impact pulse and a brief restrained creature roar synchronized with the completed slash. Keep all sounds clean, spatially coherent and synchronized with the visible action, with no clipping, hiss or distortion.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
			],
